{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics","id":424238,"title":"Telekinesis, Appropriate For Solars? Specifically, For Athletics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-01T09:41:06-08:00","id":424238,"title":"Telekinesis, Appropriate For Solars? Specifically, For Athletics","content":"So, hey, I can fly with Athletics, right? That's a thing, or did I read that series of charms wrong?<br /> <br /> So, would an appropriate extension of lifting myself off into the air with my supernal (I like that word, but I don't mean the 3e mechanic) athletics also extend to now have mind muscle to lift other stuff?<br /> <br /> And would it destroy Throw if I started chucking boulders like a steroid ridden Jedi?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T10:21:25-08:00","id":424282,"title":"","content":"hmm to be honest i personally don't think telekinesis would be the most appropriate thing for solars, in my opinion telekinesis has more of a sinister feel to it so it would probably fit better with abyssals or maybe even sidereals. My reasoning here is that solars have a tendency to go for the flashy things (in my experience) and having the ability to move/throw/crush someone or something without even moving your arms whilst awesome just doesn't have that &quot;I'm a hero&quot; feel that solar charms seem to have (i know very well that solars can be some of the worst people in creation but their charms where made to be &quot;heroic&quot; not &quot;villainous&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T10:30:29-08:00","id":424292,"title":"","content":"Well, I'd involve movement, take cues from the Jedi and all that, plus <i>Athletics.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T10:37:25-08:00","id":424295,"title":"","content":"I would personally say that the Solar aesthetic is very hands on and physical; even their flight in 2e involves particular superman / wuxia wire-fu pose and all. Telekinesis just seems out of style to me, and I'm pretty sure it's been called out as such previously; a solar doesn't lift a thing across the room, he crosses the room regardless of intervening obstacles and lifts it regardless of its' weight and what should be keeping it in place; that is solar athletics to me. Doing what should be impossible (crossing a death trap to rip a pillar out of place and throw it), but technically is possible (well, the death trap COULD be crossed but no man could make those jumps or survive those obstacles, and the pillar COULD be moved but no man is strong enough for the task).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T10:41:10-08:00","id":424297,"title":"","content":"I don't see Telekenesis being a very Solar thing, and particularly not in Athletics. Their entire charm set is about being mind-bogglingly good at things to the point they can do things that appear superhuman. They can fly because they have become so good at jumping that they can pull a Douglas Adams and dodge the ground. There aren't really any charms that would cascade into that style of power, either. Take, for example, Superman. Honestly one of the better examples of a Solar, he's just naturally so good he can lift a car and leap a building in a single bound, but even in his ridiculously long run, Telekenesis was never a thing he's been given.<br /> <br /> That being said, I could see a Blood Bending style faux telekenesis for Abyssals, but they're whole style is drastically different anyway","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T10:45:48-08:00","id":424303,"title":"","content":"What muddles the issue is that Solars (in 2ed) are <i>not</i> strictly &quot;human skills up to 11&quot;, because at several points, they just... well, do weird stuff. Like create weapons out of energy. Walk on walls and ceilings. Shoot energy bolts. Fly.<br /> <br /> I am not <i>sure</i> whether I like that.<br /> <br /> I could see them doing jedi-style telekinesis - pulling or pushing stuff they can't actually reach. It's not any more weird than flying. But then, I don't really like that they can fly. In fact, I'm already thorn about the energy bolts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T11:14:52-08:00","id":424318,"title":"","content":"Telekinesis <i>can</i> be in-theme for Solars (see Iron Raptor Technique), but it would stem from the mastery over the tool, such that even when away from it, it is an extension of your body (the way swords are an extra-sharp extension of your arm).<br /> <br /> So I wouldn't say Athletics qualifies, but throwing Knives (with Thrown) from a distance with a flick of the wrist, as an extension of your mastery over all thrown things, seems like it can work.<br /> <br /> Edit: said knives may or may not need to Belong to you (as per the ownership sidebar).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T11:19:00-08:00","id":424320,"title":"","content":"I think effects that seem like telekinesis are completely out of theme for the Solar, except for those Solar who plunge into the esoteric or other sorcererous arts.<br /> <br /> Solar flight shouldn't seem like telekinesis. It also shouldn't seem like Superman flight either (ye whimsical gods am I tired of hearing the Solar being compared to Superman), it's an expression of human might ascending to meet the challenge with which it contends. <br /> <br /> What I basically mean, is that when a Solar does something amazing it does not do it <i>casually</i>. A Lunar can casually turn into a bird and fly. If telekinesis were a spell any sorcerer could cast it and then casually lift whatever with their mind.<br /> <br /> The Solar does not casually do any of the amazing things they do. They expend effort, will and being; through these things they ascend.<br /> <br /> It's a human skill, in the sense what humanity (or at least some humans) do/does is rise up to meet a challenge.<br /> <br /> As for energy bolts or artifacts from nowhere, I'd go with Ki/Chi/Essence whatever being a true and existing thing in the setting as part of the reason. The Solar expresses their judgment and swordsmanship in the form of essence born trappings because that's who they are as an individual, the way a gods panoply expresses who they are as divine beings.<br /> <br /> The Solar with appropriate melee charms isn't the best mortal swordsman ever (though they could be) they are divine and incomparable expression of what it means to be a swordsman, the way myth and imagination writs it large.<br /> <br /> TLDR; these things that Solars do that seem to clash with their identity as the most human of Exalted, clash because the Solar expresses human identity in a divine and transcendent (not excellent or perfect, but specifically transcendent) way. <br /> <br /> \u200bNot necessarily the best swordsman, the divine swordsman.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T11:38:04-08:00","id":424332,"title":"","content":"Regular old telekinesis, no.<br /> <br /> The sort of tactile telekinesis where you can lift a mountain and you can lift the <i>whole thing</i> and it won't just break off one slab because of pre-existing planes of weakness? Absolutely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T11:48:46-08:00","id":424340,"title":"","content":"Well there is an athletic charm where when you fly you can take your whole army with you into the air. In fact they will mimic any athletic charm you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T11:49:48-08:00","id":424341,"title":"","content":"Just use a sorcerous working to bind an invisible air elemental to your will such that by concentrating on a given object, you appear to manipulate it remotely (via the elemental controlling the air surrounding it).<br /> <br /> Or sit in the Wyld until you have telekinesis; or sit in the Wyld until <i>you think</i> you have telekinesis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T12:29:54-08:00","id":424365,"title":"","content":"Telekinesis really only works for Solars in very specific contexts. Calling a sword to your hand isn't really telekinesis, as the sword in question is a weapon that you've bonded with and practiced with to the extent where it is considered metaphysically apart of you, you're actually just calling a piece of yourself back to yourself.<br /> <br /> Likewise with Athletics flight, it's not that you are psychically propelling yourself though the air, it's that your ability to jump and balance on impossible surfaces is such that you can do that with air currents itself. With lifting and throwing objects, the best you could get is actually grappling with a large object and throwing it without the object collapsing under it's own weight, which I think was mentioned above. Even then, that isn't proper telekinesis, it's an extension of your supernatural strength and ability to distribute weight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T12:48:20-08:00","id":424376,"title":"","content":"Oh, okay, so just me then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T12:51:51-08:00","id":424378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=424303#post424303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What muddles the issue is that Solars (in 2ed) are <i>not</i> strictly &quot;human skills up to 11&quot;, because at several points, they just... well, do weird stuff. Like create weapons out of energy. Walk on walls and ceilings. Shoot energy bolts. Fly.<br /> <br /> I am not <i>sure</i> whether I like that.<br /> <br /> I could see them doing jedi-style telekinesis - pulling or pushing stuff they can't actually reach. It's not any more weird than flying. But then, I don't really like that they can fly. In fact, I'm already thorn about the energy bolts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Solars have never been just &quot;human skills up to 11&quot; in any edition. They are also the champions of the Unconquered Sun. They wield the power of the sun itself. If the energy blast thing bothers you, remember solar flares occur in which built up energy is ejected from the sun. Walking on walls/ceilings and flying, well the sun is one of the greatest forces of gravity in the known universe. If you look at it this way, some of the Solar's stranger powers do make sense.<br /> <br /> As for telekinesis, I could see it falling in line with the gravity warping themes that some of Solar Charms inspire (looking at you &quot;flying charm&quot;). However, it's not nearly as straight forward as most Solar charms are. IE, if a Solar wants something floating in the sky, he super jumps or flies up to get it. Using telekinesis is the sort of strange meta power I'd expect a Sidereal to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T12:56:29-08:00","id":424403,"title":"","content":"No, I don't think that telekinesis in athletics is appropriate for Solars; their leaping and flying charms seem to me to revolve around internal <i>lightness</i>, not external force.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T13:23:30-08:00","id":424424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=424378#post424378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well Solars have never been just &quot;human skills up to 11&quot; in any edition. They are also the champions of the Unconquered Sun. They wield the power of the sun itself. If the energy blast thing bothers you, remember solar flares occur in which built up energy is ejected from the sun. Walking on walls/ceilings and flying, well the sun is one of the greatest forces of gravity in the known universe. If you look at it this way, some of the Solar's stranger powers do make sense.<br /> <br /> As for telekinesis, I could see it falling in line with the gravity warping themes that some of Solar Charms inspire (looking at you &quot;flying charm&quot;). However, it's not nearly as straight forward as most Solar charms are. IE, if a Solar wants something floating in the sky, he super jumps or flies up to get it. Using telekinesis is the sort of strange meta power I'd expect a Sidereal to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Gravity&quot; and &quot;Solar Flares&quot; are real-life scientific explanations, not mystical properties. It's like &quot;Pistol Shrimp Ignites The Sun Atemi&quot;. I don't even want to think in that direction.<br /> Creation doesn't revolve around TUC's sun - instead, TUC's sun travels over creation. And there are no solar flares, because why would there be?<br /> Still, I can see the light bolts as &quot;Blasting rays of holy light&quot; (because yes, TUC sheds light, and he literally defines &quot;holy&quot;), but flying... appart from &quot;Well, the sun is in the sky, so Solars can be in the sky, too&quot; (which doesn't really satisfy me), I can't really think of anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T13:33:00-08:00","id":424427,"title":"","content":"I never viewed that as flight. It really is about jumping good or basically running on air (wuxia wire-fu as others have mentioned).<br /> <br /> In terms of something like MHM, definitely no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T13:37:01-08:00","id":424433,"title":"","content":"Trying to think of ways it could fit with Solar Charm logic and Athletics, maybe a Solar who's trained and disciplined their bodily essence (they've done lots of rousing physical training montages and whatnot) could project and send their essence beyond their body and actually have it be able to lift and move things.<br /> <br /> Basically, so long as it fits via &quot;I must do chi, spiritual unification, and practice zen -&quot; route of Solars rather than something like a &quot;I am an heroic ESPer with psychic powers&quot; (which is more the Sidereal baliwick) then maybe it could work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T13:52:25-08:00","id":424446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=424433#post424433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to think of ways it could fit with Solar Charm logic and Athletics, maybe a Solar who's trained and disciplined their bodily essence (they've done lots of rousing physical training montages and whatnot) could project and send their essence beyond their body and actually have it be able to lift and move things.<br /> <br /> Basically, so long as it fits via &quot;I must do chi, spiritual unification, and practice zen -&quot; route of Solars rather than something like a &quot;I am an heroic ESPer with psychic powers&quot; (which is more the Sidereal baliwick) then maybe it could work.</div> </div> </div> </div>My follow up question to this is: does it need to fit there?<br /> <br /> Solars have pretty broad themes as it is, but they do have some constraints or thematic limits on their power, and I think that is a good thing. I really don't consider &quot;projecting my Athletics training outside of me to grab a rock&quot; to be inside the very human-ability-centric narrative of Solars. Even if you rationalize it as zen qi manipulation, I don't see it as thematically appropriate.<br /> <br /> Effects like GSS or Phantom Steed, while a little more out there, still revolve around a level of control with the Ability in question that doesn't seem to me to be present for this &quot;telekinetics in Athletics&quot; notion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 03-01-2015, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T13:57:58-08:00","id":424471,"title":"","content":"I just had another look at the charm chain.<br /> The developement is &quot;Perfect Balance on everything at least asstrong and thick as a human hair&quot; -&gt; [&quot;Perfectly Balance on surfaces of every angle&quot; &amp; &quot;Perfectly Balance on surfaces of every consistency&quot;] -&gt; &quot;Repel the ground and fly&quot;.<br /> I think they should have worded that &quot;Repel the ground&quot; as &quot;Balance in mid-air on nothing at all&quot;. But yah, that's mostly a fluff issue. It is part of the balance chain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T14:01:55-08:00","id":424480,"title":"","content":"I could think of a way to make it fit,but I wouldn't argue it as an outgrowth of athletics. Like the flying thing I see kind of fitting in on the same grounds as why Superman eventually got flight. First its a case of &quot;Not fly jump good,&quot; then it grows out into flight. Its still kind iffy on things, but I can see the outgrowth there. Telekinesis doesn't have the same feel to me that would put it in athletics. Occult though I could see it working in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T14:05:27-08:00","id":424483,"title":"","content":"Solars already have the ability to do manipulate things at a distance. It just doesn't take the form of a series of Charms building off each other to say &quot;I can move things at a distance&quot;. Instead, we have a Charm that says &quot;I am never without my weapon&quot; and lets you pick up a sword from like, way over there, and a Charm that says &quot;My cuts extend beyond my sword&quot; and lets you cut people totally far away. Along the same lines, I could see an Athletics Charm that says &quot;I can hold the Omphalos over my head while fighting off ten thousand dragon-tooth soldiers&quot; and lets you make some totally radical Anima hands to hold heavy things while you do other stuff. Throwing things you're not holding feels a little borderline, though. Not sure why.<br /> <br /> ...Hmm, actually, making yourself some huge-type Anima hands that do stuff for you while you do other stuff seems like a pretty groovy SP (Sorcerereous Projjz), if you want something a little more general purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;They&quot; is an excellent gender neutral pronoun.<br /> Avatar adapted from art by Cordell Felix <a href=\"http://cordellfelix.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://cordellfelix.com/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1177-arrghus","name":"Arrghus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1177_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T14:13:37-08:00","id":424495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=424446#post424446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My follow up question to this is: does it need to fit there?<br /> <br /> Solars have pretty broad themes as it is, but they do have some constraints or thematic limits on their power, and I think that is a good thing. I really don't consider &quot;projecting my Athletics training outside of me to grab a rock&quot; to be inside the very human-ability-centric narrative of Solars. Even if you rationalize it as zen qi manipulation, I don't see it as thematically appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm actually not convinced at all telekinesis still should be accessible via that route, as opposed to using more grounded forms of excellence, it just seemed like an interesting angle to explore how a Solar could justify an effectively telekinetic ability, where Solars are in essence like the hot blooded, rising-to-the-challenge, shonen-y spiritual martial arts guys (as filtered through pretty much any form of skill, not just martial arts) and are not really ESP masters. They do have great perception Charms and crazily strong intuition and occult sense and things that overlap with this but it's not exactly like being psychic (or even occult) as a core theme they way it is with say Sids or probably some Infernals, etc.<br /> <br /> (Like if a Solar vs a Sid were doing being Lain of the Wired, the Sid would have uncanny connectedness and harmony and distance in as a baseline assumption, while the Solar would *just* be transcendent at whatever the computer hacking equivalent of spiritual martial arts is.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T15:12:06-08:00","id":424588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=424297#post424297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take, for example, Superman. Honestly one of the better examples of a Solar, he's just naturally so good he can lift a car and leap a building in a single bound, but even in his ridiculously long run, Telekenesis was never a thing he's been given.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er, actually, starting back in 1986 the Post-Crisis explanation of Superman's powers involved solar energy-fueled psychokinesis for his flight and heat vision, and the enhanced strength and invulnerability could be extrapolated from that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T15:34:28-08:00","id":424604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=424588#post424588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Er, actually, starting back in 1986 the Post-Crisis explanation of Superman's powers involved solar energy-fueled psychokinesis for his flight and heat vision, and the enhanced strength and invulnerability could be extrapolated from that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently, the current explanation is a mix of &quot;dense body tissue&quot; and &quot;invulnerability aura&quot;. The later he can even extend to objects and people he's carrying, explaining why he can catch people after they've fallen considerable distances without them splattering on his arms, or why he can lift a car by its bumpers.<br /> Also, his clone &quot;Superboy&quot; has been given the &quot;Tactile Telekinesis&quot;-explanation for two decades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T15:45:57-08:00","id":424610,"title":"","content":"Solars get flight because, basically, without it your athletics guy would be hilariously chumped in many situations by anyone with a pair of wings. This isn't true for telekinesis -- it's not something you really <i>need</i> in and of itself.<br /> <br /> A few Solar charms might show themes you could call telekinetic, like weapons returning to your hand, thrown / archery bending to hit its target, or larceny grabbing stuff at long range, but I don't think you're likely to see Solar charms justified by telekinesis in the sense of &quot;I can do XYZ, because I'm telekinetic&quot;; instead, you might have charms that have &quot;I can do XYZ, because I'm awesome at this&quot; where XYZ is something that incidentally happens to be telekinetic.<br /> <br /> The closest stuff they're likely to have to general telekinesis would probably be in larceny rather than athletics. &quot;Manipulate things without touching them&quot; isn't an Athletics feat at all, but it could be justified as a feat of epic legerdemain and therefore fall under Larcency at times -- eg. &quot;I make that thing on the other side of the room fall over to serve as a distraction&quot; seems like a valid Solar Larcency charm to me, if slightly fringe. Even then, you would want to avoid the word telekinesis for the same reason that Solar Athletics charms can sometimes do flash step-style &quot;I'm already there, right now&quot; effects but usually avoid calling it a teleport.<br /> <br /> The other thing to consider is the various applications of telekinesis and what it makes you good at. If you have superhero-style telekinesis capable of lifting cars, crushing them into little balls, and hurling them over the horizon, that could be a problem in the Solar charmset because it doesn't fit well into their Ability-based paradigm -- that kind of telekinesis would make you exceptionally good at fighting at range, stealing things, attack, and defense, to a level that wouldn't make much sense in any one particular Solar ability tree -- Athletics is not meant to let you do Darth Vader chokes. Subtle &quot;snatch small objects&quot; or &quot;create a distraction&quot; effects, though, fit into Larcency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 03-01-2015, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T16:09:31-08:00","id":424630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=424610#post424610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars get flight because, basically, without it your athletics guy would be hilariously chumped in many situations by anyone with a pair of wings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars are limited to flying within ([Strength + Athletics] x 3) yards of a surface. That still criples them against &quot;proper&quot; fliers.<br /> <br /> A Jedi-style &quot;Force Push&quot;/&quot;Force Pull&quot;, with &quot;I'm so good at pushing/pulling/lifting things, I don't even have to touch them&quot; doesn't seem <i>that</i> far-fetched (and about as necessary as earth-bound flying) - but for proper fine manipulation, it'd have to be Largency (Actually, Largency already has similar effects, allowing a Solar to steal stuff from afar).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T16:44:30-08:00","id":424656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=424424#post424424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Gravity&quot; and &quot;Solar Flares&quot; are real-life scientific explanations, not mystical properties. It's like &quot;Pistol Shrimp Ignites The Sun Atemi&quot;. I don't even want to think in that direction.<br /> Creation doesn't revolve around TUC's sun - instead, TUC's sun travels over creation. And there are no solar flares, because why would there be?<br /> Still, I can see the light bolts as &quot;Blasting rays of holy light&quot; (because yes, TUC sheds light, and he literally defines &quot;holy&quot;), but flying... appart from &quot;Well, the sun is in the sky, so Solars can be in the sky, too&quot; (which doesn't really satisfy me), I can't really think of anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're taking far to serious of a stance here. First, I was just trying to show that there was more then one way to look at some of the Solars odder abilities. I did say it was just another way to look at things. You yourself have implied that the light blasts may be legit based only on the UCS &quot;shedding light&quot;. That itself is kind of a weak reason. I imagine the light blasts are more a Solar swordsman (or some other melee weapon) needed to strike opponents at a distance, decided to concentrate and fire blasts with his essence. A swordsman taking his skills to an obscene level at work. Just another way to explain it. I'm sure if we dedicated some real time to it, we could each come up with a few ways to explain flight as well.<br /> <br /> On a side note, the description of the Daystar (the sun) outlined in the UCS Glories stated it was constantly emitting pulses of sun-fire. Phenomenon like a solar flare are absolutely possible. Though I think we're all hoping the Daystar gets changed from the ultimate airship war machine, to something more like Luna's realm on the moon. An alternate world to explore and have new adventures!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T17:39:51-08:00","id":424697,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Dusk Shine;n424424And there are no solar flares, because why would there be?[/QUOTE]Because what in the hell did you <i>think</i> the Apollyon Cannons looked like while firing?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.nasa.gov/images/content/525037main_FAQ1-orig_full.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.nasa.gov/images/content/5...-orig_full.jpg</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T17:51:29-08:00","id":424713,"title":"","content":"&quot;Telekinesis&quot; doesn\u2019t really work for Solars for the same reason \u201celectromagnetic manipulation\u201d doesn\u2019t work. It sounds science fiction-y. That said, you can cause five hundred swords to fly through the air at your enemy and shine with brilliant light.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=424446#post424446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My follow up question to this is: does it need to fit there?<br /> <br /> Effects like GSS or Phantom Steed, while a little more out there, still revolve around a level of control with the Ability in question that doesn't seem to me to be present for this &quot;telekinetics in Athletics&quot; notion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The examples given were using telekinesis to chuck around boulders and leap through the air. Both of those fit into athletics.<br /> <br /> If you were using your telekinetics to block attacks, it would be Brawl. If you were using it to maintain the integrity of your ship during a storm, it would be Sail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 03-01-2015, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T18:30:35-08:00","id":424734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrghus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=424483#post424483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Hmm, actually, making yourself some huge-type Anima hands that do stuff for you while you do other stuff seems like a pretty groovy SP (Sorcerereous Projjz), if you want something a little more general purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=424341#post424341\">*cough, cough*</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-01-2015, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T19:27:24-08:00","id":424756,"title":"","content":"I'm personally of the opinion that they shouldn't be able to fly in the first place and hope it ceases to be a thing in 3E. Also, they pretty blatantly tossed it in because 'Superman seems solar like and he can fly so lets let solars fly'. You can tell because the charm literally requires you to do his iconic 'one fist forward' flight pose to use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T23:33:19-08:00","id":424916,"title":"","content":"Tl;dr Mortals use their souls to manipulate essence. Solars turn that skill to 11 with the aid of their anima banner, a physical feature unique to the exalted that allows them to magically manipulate their environment. They're super-enlightened-mortals.<br /> <br /> The mini-rant on my head canon:<br /> To me at least, the anima banner is the real, physical manifestation of the exalt's soul. That's why it's individualized to reflect them. I've seen stunts where a bird totem flapped to give the exalt lift in their jump.<br /> <br /> Outside of stunts, what do you think is happening when you use Call the Blade? You're using the invisible (sometimes visible) anima banner to pull the blade in. You tie up a large portion of your anima's power in attuning (lifting!) extraordinarily heavy artifacts. And yes, enlightened solars can grip stuff with their (invisible!) anima banners.<br /> <br /> Enlightenment progresses an exalt's control of anima-based telekinesis from resonant orichalcum artifacts to learned, limited telekinesis and straight through bizarre flight and more. They're super humanly skilled at manipulating the world through a magical set of invisible limbs.<br /> <br /> In my mind, the anima is what makes all of the exalted so powerful. The rest of the world doesn't have the soul extension (metaphysical super strength) the exaltation grants. They have to deal with a soul that doesn't have the structure (limbs) built for heavy lifting.<br /> <br /> Note: Straight telekinesis is difficult, requiring high enlightenment (essence). It's not popular in combat. Why go through the effort of fighting without spiritual leverage when you can fight enemies directly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":4729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","user":"Childofthesun1","date":". 03-02-2015, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T00:04:12-08:00","id":424939,"title":"","content":"I think full on telekinesis is out of theme for Solar Exalted, though limited uses of it are probably appropriate for Thrown, allowing you to redirect or move things in mid-flight.<br /> <br /> I just can't see Telekinesis as Athletics.<br /> <br /> I could certainly see Telekinesis is in-theme for Abyssals though, with the idea of poltergeists moving stuff around and what not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T06:59:48-08:00","id":425126,"title":"","content":"I would make TK an Occult Cham. Use permanent Essence as the effective Str score and manipulate or target with Perception + Occult. Gives me the image of a classic wizards hand spell which in appropriate fiction is a pretty common ability among occultists. I wouldnt even make it a sorcery spell (maybe a far more powerful version) just Occult and pretty much make it availablle to most splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T07:14:47-08:00","id":425156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrghus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=424483#post424483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars already have the ability to do manipulate things at a distance. It just doesn't take the form of a series of Charms building off each other to say &amp;quot;I can move things at a distance&amp;quot;. Instead, we have a Charm that says &amp;quot;I am never without my weapon&amp;quot; and lets you pick up a sword from like, way over there, and a Charm that says &amp;quot;My cuts extend beyond my sword&amp;quot; and lets you cut people totally far away. Along the same lines, I could see an Athletics Charm that says &amp;quot;I can hold the Omphalos over my head while fighting off ten thousand dragon-tooth soldiers&amp;quot; and lets you make some totally radical Anima hands to hold heavy things while you do other stuff. Throwing things you're not holding feels a little borderline, though. Not sure why.<br /> <br /> ...Hmm, actually, making yourself some huge-type Anima hands that do stuff for you while you do other stuff seems like a pretty groovy SP (Sorcerereous Projjz), if you want something a little more general purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention that Iron Raptor Technique lets you telekinetically wield your weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T07:32:34-08:00","id":425166,"title":"","content":"What's the Essence requirement for the Flight charm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5154-cappadocius","name":"cappadocius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T07:59:53-08:00","id":425199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=425156#post425156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to mention that Iron Raptor Technique lets you telekinetically wield your weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not entirely accurate. It flies out for 1 attack and returns to your hand immediately. It can be seen as a &quot;boomerang sword&quot; technique, without any actual telekinesis. But yeah, as I mentioned earlier, for solars it'd be more in the scope of &quot;mastered a weapon group such that they [obey me/are an extension of me] even from a distance&quot; rather than &quot;so good at lifting that I lift ALL the things&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T08:22:34-08:00","id":425236,"title":"","content":"WHY AM I JUST NOW REALIZING I CAN MAKE A SOLAR THAT FIGHTS LIKE CAPTAIN AMERICA!?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1238-crimyote","name":"Crimyote","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T08:24:16-08:00","id":425237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=425126#post425126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would make TK an Occult Cham. Use permanent Essence as the effective Str score and manipulate or target with Perception + Occult. Gives me the image of a classic wizards hand spell which in appropriate fiction is a pretty common ability among occultists. I wouldnt even make it a sorcery spell (maybe a far more powerful version) just Occult and pretty much make it availablle to most splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Somehow, I don't think that the likely stowing place for Mind-Hand Manipulation will bear the same fruit for Solars that it does for Infernals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T08:27:23-08:00","id":425240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crimyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=425236#post425236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WHY AM I JUST NOW REALIZING I CAN MAKE A SOLAR THAT FIGHTS LIKE CAPTAIN AMERICA!?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell if I know - the rest of us figured it out back when Thunderbolt Shields were errata'ed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T10:11:12-08:00","id":425377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=424756#post424756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm personally of the opinion that they shouldn't be able to fly in the first place and hope it ceases to be a thing in 3E. Also, they pretty blatantly tossed it in because 'Superman seems solar like and he can fly so lets let solars fly'. You can tell because the charm literally requires you to do his iconic 'one fist forward' flight pose to use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would actually be shocked if this were the case. Ignoring gravity via wuxia goodness is too much in theme for Exalted in general for Solars not to have it. If anything, I'm expecting more of the Exalted host to have access to some type of flight based charm. air or fire bursts for Dragonblooded, to propel themselves, growing skeletal wings out or their own shadows for Abyssals, and just straight up pushing the &quot;off&quot; button on gravity for Sidereals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T10:53:52-08:00","id":425422,"title":"","content":"I am <i>sure</i> I once found an &quot;Solar shoots holy lazors out of their caste mark&quot; charm. I think it was in occult. Maybe an Abyssal charm that was mirrored? Anyway, I <i>would</i> hold it as an example for &quot;Yes, sometimes Solars simply glow like the sun, and burn others in the process&quot;... if I could find the thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T11:31:51-08:00","id":425448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=425422#post425422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am <i>sure</i> I once found an &quot;Solar shoots holy lazors out of their caste mark&quot; charm. I think it was in occult. Maybe an Abyssal charm that was mirrored? Anyway, I <i>would</i> hold it as an example for &quot;Yes, sometimes Solars simply glow like the sun, and burn others in the process&quot;... if I could find the thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that Blazing Solar Bolt? (I could be thinking of 1e. I haven't played an actual game in so long that the two editions are starting to meld within my memories).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T11:53:12-08:00","id":425467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=425448#post425448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that Blazing Solar Bolt?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. BSB does say the Solar's caste mark blazes, but then your weapon catches fire and you can now melee at a distance by throwing that fire at enemies.<br /> What I was refering to was an actual &quot;beam attack&quot; coming out of the caste mark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T12:02:26-08:00","id":425503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=425422#post425422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am <i>sure</i> I once found an &amp;quot;Solar shoots holy lazors out of their caste mark&amp;quot; charm. I think it was in occult. Maybe an Abyssal charm that was mirrored? Anyway, I <i>would</i> hold it as an example for &amp;quot;Yes, sometimes Solars simply glow like the sun, and burn others in the process&amp;quot;... if I could find the thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Caste Book Zenith had survival charms for tossing out fire lasers. They build off of 'start campfire perfectly' and then 'make permanent or blazing campfire' and finally 'shoot fire from your eyes.'<br /> <br /> I think that's the flow of it, it's been kind of a long while since I perused it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T12:23:25-08:00","id":425537,"title":"","content":"Couldn't be that, either. I barely touched the 1ed books.<br /> <br /> I might confuse &quot;Eyes Like Daggers Glance&quot; (which allows <i>Abyssals</i> to shoot attacks from their eyes) with its mirror &quot;Fiery Solar Chakram&quot;, which allows Solars to attack with &quot;spiritual weapons&quot; using Charisma instead of Dexterity - but they still have to use their hands to use the weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T13:03:25-08:00","id":425582,"title":"","content":"Okay, slightly new tact.<br /> <br /> Would it be appropriate for &quot;that one Solar&quot; to have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T13:11:42-08:00","id":425597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=425582#post425582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, slightly new tact.<br /> <br /> Would it be appropriate for &quot;that one Solar&quot; to have?</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO, absolutely. Properly filtered through esoteric understandings of Solar essence, it's perfectly appropriate. Solars ignore petty limits on their capabilities, up to and including needing to grip something to lift it. Flavor with anima or whatever as appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T13:22:47-08:00","id":425606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=425503#post425503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Caste Book Zenith had survival charms for tossing out fire lasers. They build off of 'start campfire perfectly' and then 'make permanent or blazing campfire' and finally 'shoot fire from your eyes.'<br /> <br /> I think that's the flow of it, it's been kind of a long while since I perused it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it went from &quot;scratch together fires on dry wood&quot; to &quot;light fires by clapping or making some other kind of gesture, even on stone&quot; to &quot;fire down from the sky, anywhere outdoors that you can see&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T13:44:23-08:00","id":425631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=425199#post425199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not entirely accurate. It flies out for 1 attack and returns to your hand immediately. It can be seen as a &quot;boomerang sword&quot; technique, without any actual telekinesis. But yeah, as I mentioned earlier, for solars it'd be more in the scope of &quot;mastered a weapon group such that they [obey me/are an extension of me] even from a distance&quot; rather than &quot;so good at lifting that I lift ALL the things&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, until you combo that charm with an extra action charm, then your weapon flies out and attacks an opponent 6 times before it comes back and it starts looking a whole lot like TK. Not to mention that Iron Raptor flows from Call the Blade, which also really looks like Telekinesis. Also, Iron Raptor can be upgraded to Sandstorm Wind Attack (or in 1st ed, it flows from iron raptor as its own charm), which looks a whole lot like a telekinetic cut.<br /> <br /> Just sayin.<br /> <br /> But yeah i get where your coming from and it looks to me that is what the designers intended as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":779,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","user":"NuSoardGraphite","date":". 03-02-2015, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T13:51:20-08:00","id":425639,"title":"","content":"Or it could be that you fling the weapon out six times, and it returns to your hand six times, at which point it continues to not be TK and is just boomeranging <i>really damn fast</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T14:35:12-08:00","id":425691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=425377#post425377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would actually be shocked if this were the case. Ignoring gravity via wuxia goodness is too much in theme for Exalted in general for Solars not to have it. If anything, I'm expecting more of the Exalted host to have access to some type of flight based charm. air or fire bursts for Dragonblooded, to propel themselves, growing skeletal wings out or their own shadows for Abyssals, and just straight up pushing the &quot;off&quot; button on gravity for Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the very least if they keep it I would like them to remove the mechanically enforced superman shout out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T16:08:41-08:00","id":425750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=425606#post425606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it went from &quot;scratch together fires on dry wood&quot; to &quot;light fires by clapping or making some other kind of gesture, even on stone&quot; to &quot;fire down from the sky, anywhere outdoors that you can see&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aha, that's it! Thanks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T17:26:08-08:00","id":425822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=425639#post425639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or it could be that you fling the weapon out six times, and it returns to your hand six times, at which point it continues to not be TK and is just boomeranging <i>really damn fast</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This pretty much sums up how myself and everyone I've gamed with pictures/understands flurries and Iron Raptor to work. Strider Hein from Strider 2 was one of my earliest inspirations for combining the two things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HgZzQokC0Qo\" data-code=\"HgZzQokC0Qo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/HgZzQokC0Qo/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T19:06:34-08:00","id":426039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=425691#post425691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At the very least if they keep it I would like them to remove the mechanically enforced superman shout out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently, that was more intended to be the wuxia wire-fu pose than Superman, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T20:59:27-08:00","id":426133,"title":"","content":"So i was perusing clips of wuxia movies on youtube because i have seen literally hundreds of these movies and i have seen many examples of characters using TK to wield their weapons, which is my perception of how Iron Raptor works. Its not that i dont think that iron raptorn could represent a thrown sword, that is then called back via call the blade or boomerangs, it absolutely could, i just like the image of a TK weilded weapon better. Its a personal preferrence. I just wanted a video to show my perspective.<br /> <br /> And i found this absolutely beautiful clip from Return of the Condor Heroes, which i actually havent seen, and the fight is all Exalted. The female character in this clip is truly INVINCIBLE SWORD PRINCESS made manifest. She battles a character who uses Iron Raptor with a shield, and even combos it with an extra action charm. At first it looks like he is throwing the shield, then later in the fight, he straight up TKs it! Both work in the context of this clip. Check this scene out btw, its worth every second.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://youtu.be/Ftf0VDTtCuI\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://youtu.be/Ftf0VDTtCuI\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://youtu.be/Ftf0VDTtCuI\" target=\"_blank\"> http://youtu.be/Ftf0VDTtCuI </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T21:03:42-08:00","id":426134,"title":"","content":"In order for a &quot;telekinesis&quot; effect to flow naturally from the Abilities of the Solar Exalted, it needs to make sense within the actual and symbolic context of that Ability. This is why Call the Blade works as a Solar Melee Charm. You can't treat Charms as scientific phenomena and derive new Charms from that\u2014Eagle-Wing Style won't generalize into actual psychic telekinesis any more than Racing Hare Method will let the Solar do bullshit like stealing speed from people. That's how the Flash works. Solars aren't superheroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T21:07:41-08:00","id":426139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=425691#post425691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the very least if they keep it I would like them to remove the mechanically enforced superman shout out.</div> </div> </div> </div>If memory serves, the pose was intended to prevent the game breaking effect of flying around and raining death from above with impunity. I suspect that 3e will have a more elegant solution than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T21:09:12-08:00","id":426140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=426134#post426134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In order for a &amp;quot;telekinesis&amp;quot; effect to flow naturally from the Abilities of the Solar Exalted, it needs to make sense within the actual and symbolic context of that Ability. This is why Call the Blade works as a Solar Melee Charm. You can't treat Charms as scientific phenomena and derive new Charms from that\u2014Eagle-Wing Style won't generalize into actual psychic telekinesis any more than Racing Hare Method will let the Solar do bullshit like stealing speed from people. That's how the Flash works. Solars aren't superheroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats why i suggest placing TK into Occult, representing the fact that using invisible magical hand with a long reach is actually a very, very common feat in the source material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T22:03:02-08:00","id":426180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=426140#post426140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thats why i suggest placing TK into Occult, representing the fact that using invisible magical hand with a long reach is actually a very, very common feat in the source material.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how &quot;invisible magical hand&quot; arises naturally from Occult. A spell, sure, but the Ability of esoteric rituals and otherworldly lore does not seem very prone to kineticism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T22:15:36-08:00","id":426194,"title":"","content":"So, Bobby, as I suggested earlier, what about it being something &quot;that one solar&quot; does?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T22:25:54-08:00","id":426206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=426180#post426180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how &amp;quot;invisible magical hand&amp;quot; arises naturally from Occult. A spell, sure, but the Ability of esoteric rituals and otherworldly lore does not seem very prone to kineticism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I say it rises naturally from Occult because it is such a common magical ability in the source material. It seems to be easy to do without much effort, which makes me think Charm, rather than spell, but of course a Charm version shouldnt be uber powerful, just useful. I would totay be okay with a Sorcery version which is VASTLY more poweful, rather than just being able to loft a boulder or a single enemy, the Sorcerer could lift a giant behemoth, or an entire village or a Thousand Forged Dragon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T01:32:50-08:00","id":426282,"title":"","content":"My idea of a fitting charm line would flow like this: <br /> 1.: I am good at lifting/pushing/pulling things <br /> 2.: I can now lift/pull/push things without breaking them, even when they should (like swinging a brittle pillar or holding a yeddim up by its tail) <br /> 3.: I now don't even need proper grip to do so, any touch is enough<br /> 4.: I don't even need to touch as long as I'm close enough","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T01:58:51-08:00","id":426297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=426206#post426206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I say it rises naturally from Occult because it is such a common magical ability in the source material. It seems to be easy to do without much effort, which makes me think Charm, rather than spell, but of course a Charm version shouldnt be uber powerful, just useful. I would totay be okay with a Sorcery version which is VASTLY more poweful, rather than just being able to loft a boulder or a single enemy, the Sorcerer could lift a giant behemoth, or an entire village or a Thousand Forged Dragon.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Occult got everything that was portrayed as magic, it'd swallow up a whole bunch of Charms from other Abilities. Occult is the skill of exorcists who lay down salt lines against the restless dead, infernalists, shamans who venture through the Wyld, a village wise woman with a knack for thaumaturgy, or, occasionally, a motherfucking sorcerer. Any Occult Charms need to arise from that logic. <br /> <br /> Overall, I don't think that a generalized telekinesis effect in the style of Mind-Hand Manipulation is going to be something that ever appears in Solar Charms, but that their overall ability to exert telekinetic force, or act as though they were doing so telekinetically, is as high as it needs to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T02:01:19-08:00","id":426301,"title":"","content":"Can you use a sorcerous working to give yourself telekinesis? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:White\">We both know the answer to that.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-03-2015, 05:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T09:39:55-08:00","id":426638,"title":"","content":"As a Solar fan, I would object loudly if Telekinesis somehow made it's way in to the Solar Charmset without it being a Sorcerous Working or some other form of external power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T10:44:52-08:00","id":426700,"title":"","content":"Solars have TK when it implies mastery. It would unlikely be a function of any one particular Ability. Call the Blade, for instance, causes a weapon to fly to one's hand.<br /> <br /> Athletics may, indeed, have the ability to lift something without the proper leverage to hold it together.<br /> <br /> Larceny could allow lockpicking without having to reach inside the lock, or pickpocketing without having to actually touch the pocket-bearer.<br /> <br /> Stealth may have loud, noisy objects move out of the way, and obscuring objects move to interpose themselves.<br /> <br /> Presence could have dramatic environmental flourishes - doors flying open, dance partners being pulled in a slide into one's arms, sheer force of personality literally pressing against onlookers - accompany the absolute, well, Presence of the Solar.<br /> <br /> Though this creeps into Abyssal themes, Resistance might allow telekinetic control of severed body parts, as the Exalt's will resists even disconnection.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T20:25:03-08:00","id":427293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yzarc</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember a comment on a Solar just making a ring of TK and its evocations, but unfortunately I can't find the quote. Also I may be misremembering this so I am not too sure on it.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/YzFyM6F.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T21:33:54-08:00","id":427402,"title":"","content":"Every time I forget how much I fuckin' hate Hal Jordan, someone reminds me. I never thought it would be Vance, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T21:50:43-08:00","id":427442,"title":"","content":"To be fair, Green Lanterns are all kinda idiots who do more or less the same thing. Comes with the perils of writing a character who's too powerful, you gotta nerf them in some way or else there wont be any tension or drama. Usually that nerf comes in the form of a intelligence drop. See also the Flash in the JLU show","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T21:59:49-08:00","id":427446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=427442#post427442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, Green Lanterns are all kinda idiots who do more or less the same thing. Comes with the perils of writing a character who's too powerful, you gotta nerf them in some way or else there wont be any tension or drama. Usually that nerf comes in the form of a intelligence drop. See also the Flash in the JLU show</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, you have a character like Batman, who is so powerless compared to the rest of the JLA that his tech and mental abilities are buffed to the moon in back. I recall the time it took him about five minutes to rig a single A/C in an apartment building such that the entire building's temperature plunged to absolute zero, freezing the alien swarm within.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s no different than \u201cAnd then Superman used his super-breath to freeze them all,\u201d only the power is derived from genius-osity instead of yellow sun radiation. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T22:04:54-08:00","id":427450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=427446#post427446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alternatively, you have a character like Batman, who is so powerless compared to the rest of the JLA that his tech and mental abilities are buffed to the moon in back. I recall the time it took him about five minutes to rig a single A/C in an apartment building such that the entire building's temperature plunged to absolute zero, freezing the alien swarm within.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s no different than \u201cAnd then Superman used his super-breath to freeze them all,\u201d only the power is derived from genius-osity instead of yellow sun radiation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much, yeah. This is why I hold the opinion that the more powerful members of the DC/Marvel comic universes need to be either nerfed hard or have their powers reworked in such a way that allows the writers to present them with challenges that aren't automatically world endangering, and allow the more down to earth heroes an opportunity to shine without resorting to ridiculous things like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T22:48:51-08:00","id":427467,"title":"","content":"For me, it's not the varied power levels that are the problem but the need for everyone to live in the same universe and have semi-annual crossovers.<br /> <br /> Something that's a challenge to Thor will crush Spider-Man like a bug. That works! Spider-Man fits perfectly in a world where there are things that could use him for butt floss. The next time the Avengers decide to travel to an alien world to fight a planet devouring horde, Spider-Man can be like, &quot;Have fun guys! I'll beat up Doc Ock if he tries to break into the Avenger tower while you're away.&quot;<br /> <br /> It just that there's an editorial mandate for popular characters* to get shoe-horned into stories that don't really fit them.<br /> <br /> * Or for all character to get stuffed into event storylines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T00:15:30-08:00","id":427499,"title":"","content":"People like more than one hero, and like watching them team up and go on cool adventures, so I don't think that will ever go away. Bringing down the power level of certain heroes would solve a lot of issues with that, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T08:45:19-08:00","id":427757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/424238-telekinesis-appropriate-for-solars-specifically-for-athletics?p=426180#post426180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how &quot;invisible magical hand&quot; arises naturally from Occult. A spell, sure, but the Ability of esoteric rituals and otherworldly lore does not seem very prone to kineticism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think most of it is that people want Solar Occult charms to be good for things besides messing around with spirits. I mean really, that was pretty much the only thing 2e Occult was good for aside from getting access to the charm sets of other splats; you had the see spirits charm, the cut spirits charm, the kill spirits charm, the make spirits go away charm, the have-a-tea-party-with-a-spirit charm, and the whole tree was pretty useless for someone who just wanted to have super-thaumaturgy or charms that interacted to any degree at all with Sorcery. The only exception was AESS and Sorcerer's Burning Chakram, both essence 4+ charms that only enhanced your senses as opposed to your ability to <i>do stuff</i> with Occult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T08:48:18-08:00","id":427759,"title":"","content":"I always thought it would be neat to have a &quot;Sorcerer Needs No Tools&quot; Charm that allows you do perform mortal thaumaturgy without materials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T09:05:43-08:00","id":427776,"title":"","content":"Pre-errata, that was just called &quot;spending a mote.&quot; Then they errata'ed it because of how problematic it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}